Expected elements: present

All must-shows verified; no must-not-show present. Light here is dense, hairline, monospace-led — not a marketing surface, so no register error. Most text is strong (6.3–19:1). The failures are role discipline and state emphasis.

Glyph verdict (the open question): exactly two instances in the viewport. `⊘` at (74–83, 291–299), core #484848 on #FFFFFF = **9.15:1**. `⊙` at (74–83, 360–368), core #0E7490 on band #A5F3FC = **4.29:1** — up from the reported 2.40:1, but zero pixels reach 4.5:1. The rings are pixel-identical; the interiors are not "two pixels apart" — `⊘` carries a corner-to-corner diagonal touching both walls, `⊙` an isolated 2×3 central pip. Desaturated at 1× and at 14× they read as a barred ring versus a target. **Distinguishable without colour: yes — with zero margin.** The pip survives on a single-pixel counter each side; any fractional DPR or heavier weight closes it. `⊙` also shares its cyan with the twenty neutral `·` coverage marks (#1A7B95).

Systemic: "current" is the lowest-contrast state in every triad — iteration chip `3` #164E63 on #919191 = 2.89:1 versus completed 4.93:1; current-line rule outer #0E7490 5.36:1 versus the not-taken rule's #484848 9.15:1.

Top fixes: raise every "current" token above its "done"/"not-run" sibling; stop sharing hexes between editor tokens and status roles (#166534, #155E75).

Rating: 6/10

